# __NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

Generated from [`@provin-line/create-policy-verifier`](https://github.com/provin-line/auth/tree/develop/packages/create-policy-verifier).
It wraps [`@o3co/auth.policy-verifier.server`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@o3co/auth.policy-verifier.server)
and preregisters the dPLaaX attribute and rule collectors from
[`@provin-line/policy-verifier-dplaax-module`](https://github.com/provin-line/auth/tree/develop/packages/policy-verifier-dplaax-module).

## Quick start

```bash
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ install
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run build
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run start
```

The service listens on `http://0.0.0.0:__PORT__` by default. Override with
`HTTP_HOSTNAME` and `HTTP_PORT`.

Run the test suite:

```bash
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run test
```

## Customize

| Where | What |
| --- | --- |
| `config/application.conf` | Base attribute + rule collector lists. Add deployment-specific entries to `rule.collectors[].rules`. |
| `config/development.conf` / `config/production.conf` | Per-environment overlays merged via HOCON `withFallback`. |
| `src/rules/` | Project-specific `RuleCollector` implementations. Register them in `src/main.mts`. |
| `src/collectors/` | Project-specific `AttributeCollector` implementations. Same wiring. |

Per dPLaaX auth spec § 2, this verifier is L1-only; Pipeline Chain
connection authentication runs on L2 wire signing and bypasses this
service entirely. Avoid declaring `registry.chain.peer.*` rules — the
default test in `src/__tests__/config/configFiles.test.mts` enforces
that pin.

## Docker

```bash
make docker                # build runtime image
make docker-compose-up     # local stack via docker-compose.yml
```

## Package manager

This scaffold uses pnpm (see `packageManager` in `package.json`) because
the dPLaaX module dep is pinned via pnpm's git-subdirectory syntax,
which is not npm-compatible. Override at your own risk.

